    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="b333817c-7428-5654-8253-2b1c79bc0c8a" activityNameId="57221518-af5d-50c1-ae5f-8186f514615c" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Slurry store and processing, operation</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Slurry store and processing, operation
The module includes the use of energy and auxiliary materials for the operation of marine screw agitator. The functional unit is m3 slurry.;
UUID: 23d239a1-9923-3c51-97bb-8692725b196d
The inventory takes into account the energy and auxiliary materials like water, lubricating oil and cleaning agents. Also included is the use of the infrastructure. Not taken into account were the direct emission of the animal husbandry, fodder production and produced waste water.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: The use of energy and auxiliary materials are calculated for the conditions defined in the infrastructure-module with literature data and experts knowledge.
Time period: Period indicated in the reference. 
Production volume: Existing slurry store volume in CH in 1996: 14'847'685 m3.
Sampling: In the use of energy and auxiliary materials are big differences between the farms. The inventory is based on mean values from CH and WEU. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_23d239a1-9923-3c51-97bb-8692725b196d.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
